<div id="dropdown-menu-10" class="dropdown-menu">
 <h2>How it works</h2>
 <p class="mb-4">
  See -
  <code
   >css/root/_base-color.scss, css/root/_variables.scss, css/root/mixins,
   css/class/...all</code
  >
 </p>
 <p class="mb-4">
  The <em>_class-helpers.scss</em> imports all the <em>partials</em> and runs
  them through a mixin to generate classes adding
  <em>breakpoints, color</em> and <em>spacing</em> where necessary
 </p>
 <p>
  The color palette is from <a href="https://tailwindcss.com">Tailwind</a>. To
  use the colors is simple, being <em>color name and shade</em> eg
  <em>blue-500</em>. Precede it with what you want to color eg
  <em>text-, bg- or border-</em>. Add a <em>breakpoint</em> or <em>hover</em>.
 </p>
 <pre><code>//examples
//text
text-blue-400
text-slate-200

//background color
bg-blue-400
bg-slate-200

//border
border-blue-400
border-slate-200

//color variables
//$variables don't change on dark mode
//var(--variables) change with dark mode
//use text-, bg- or border with the variables
text-dark-gray - $dark-gray
bg-medium-gray - $medium-gray
border-light-gray - $light-gray
text-first-color - $first-color
bg-second-color - $second-color
border-font-color - var(--font-color)
text-link-color - var(--link-color)
text-hover-color - var(--hover-color)
bg-page-bg - var(--viewport-bg)
bg-bg - var(--bg)
bg-light-bg - var(--light-bg)
border-black - $black
text-white - $white
text- error - $error
bg-alert - $alert
border-success - $success

//breakpoints
$medium: 768px; class - _m
$large: 1024px; class - _l
$xlarge: 1200px; class - _xl
$wide: 1440px; class - _w

//usage
bg-blue-400_l
bg-link-color_xl
text-slate-200_m
border-medium-gray_w

//hovers
hover-text-blue-300
hover-text-success// variable

hover-bg-blue-300
hover-bg-success// variable

hover-border-blue-300
hover-border-success// variable</code></pre>

 <h3>Spacing</h3>
 <p class="mb-2">
  Spacing works with the <code>$s-0 to $s-15 in the _variables.scss</code>. See
  the <code>css/class/_spacing.scss</code> file
 </p>
 <p class="mb-4">
  The <em>margin, padding, width, height and gap</em> take the spacing values
 </p>

 <pre><code>//the spacing variables
0 - $s-0 - 0
1 - $s-1 - 0.25rem
2 - $s-2 - 0.5rem
3 - $s-3 - 0.75rem
4 - $s-4 - 1rem
5 - $s-5 - 1.25rem
6 - $s-6 - 1.5rem
7 - $s-7 - 1.75rem
8 - $s-8 - 2rem
9 - $s-9 - 2.25rem
10 - $s-10 - 3rem
11 - $s-11 - 3.5rem
12 - $s-12 - 4rem
13 - $s-13 - 4.5rem
14 - $s-14 - 5rem
15 - $s-15 - 5.5rem
auto - auto //class only</code></pre>

 <pre><code class="language-scss">//spacing class examples
//margin
m-3 - margin: 0.75rem;
my-6 - margin-block: 1.5rem;
mx-auto - margin-inline: auto;
mt-5 - margin-top: 1.25rem;
mb-4 - margin-bottom: 1rem;
ms-2 - margin-inline-start: 0.5rem;
me-6 - margin-inline-end: 1.5rem;

//padding
p-3 - padding: 0.75rem;
py-6 - padding-block: 1.5rem;
px-12 - padding-inline: 4rem;
pt-5 - padding-top: 1.25rem;
pb-4 - padding-bottom: 1rem;
ps-2 - padding-inline-start: 0.5rem;
pe-6 - padding-inline-end: 1.5rem;

//width and height
w-0 - width: 0;
w-2 - width: 0.5rem;
w-6 - width: 1.5rem;
h-8 - height: 2rem;
h-10 - height: 3rem;
h-15 - height: 5.5rem

//gap
gap-6 - gap: 1.5rem;
row-gap-7 row-gap: 1.75rem;
col-gap-3 column-gap: 0.75rem;</code></pre>

 <pre><code>//usage of utilities classes
&lt;div class="p-8 bg-slate-100 m-4"&gt;
&lt;h1 class="mb-4 text-blue-900"&gt;Hello World&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p class="ps-2 text-slate-700"&gt;This has a left padding of 0.5rem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;a href="#" class="my-2 text-rose-400 hover-text-rose-800"&gt;This link goes nowhere&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
